WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.200
Welcome to Guiding People Through Change: Facilitator Learning

00:00:03.280 --> 00:00:06.960
Path. I’m Brian Kennedy Jr. This introduction will

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:09.200
help you put the workbook to use. You

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:11.920
will work toward a listening plan, practical next-step

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:15.680
conversation and a bounded teach-back. Ask what is

00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:18.000
changing for the person and what support they

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:22.080
say they need. Practice listening without diagnosing, prescribing

00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:25.360
or assuming one reaction fits everyone. Choose a

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:28.000
real situation you can work on privately, or

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:30.800
use a clearly labeled fictional example. You can

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:33.840
write, speak your response or use another accessible

00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:36.480
format. As you work, keep a record of

00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:38.720
what you tried, what you noticed and what

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:41.840
you changed. The useful result is a facilitator

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:45.280
conversation and referral-boundary plan, with enough detail that

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:48.800
you can explain your next step. Educational facilitation

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:53.680
only; no therapy, counseling-grade claim, accredited certification or

00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:57.920
unverified degree specialization. Begin with the starting reflection

00:00:57.960 --> 00:01:00.560
in your workbook. Name the decision or practice

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:02.560
you want help with, set a review date,

00:01:02.840 --> 00:01:04.320
and open the first exercise.
